      },
      "text": "Teams are the primary unit of knowledge work. The research on what makes teams effective is more solid than most leadership research — particularly the work on psychological safety, which has survived large-scale empirical testing. Understanding team failure modes (social loafing, groupthink, fault lines) is as important as understanding what enables performance."
